    data_preparation/preprocess.py
        Raw MLII ecg -----> filtered ecg

    1.Baseline-wander removal
        Real ECG signals can slowly move up and down because of:
            *respiration
            *electrode movement
            *body movement
            *electrode contact changes

    2.Low-pass filtering
        *High frequency noise can be present in ecgs
        *Low-pass filter allows the important ecg frequency component  through it while reducing the            unwanted high frequency noise

    3.50 Hz notch filtering
        *for India , electric main frequency is 50Hz
        * it will interfrence this

    4.Normalization
        *The neural network generally benefits from a consistent input scale.


